 succeeded in 0ms:
# Checkpoint — zombie FPS (clean room, zombie-fps-local-ai)

## TASK
Build/verify the FPS in THIS folder per GAME_GOAL.md + AGENTS.md; when it genuinely works, write REPORT.md and STOP.
Immutable constraints:
- RULE ZERO: internal consistency is NOT evidence. Prove orientation from SCREEN-SPACE PROJECTION (ndc signs / projected screen coords), not from internal numbers agreeing.
- Clean room: never read/copy code from other projects (esp. old fps-grid-calibration). Three.js local only (./three.module.js), no CDN/external assets.
- Blocking defects (must have none): reversed W/S or A/D; movement not camera-relative after turning; crosshair not at exact viewport centre; crosshair-to-hit misalignment; zombie dying on 4th or surviving 5th valid hit; fatal page errors.
- Movement: W = camera forward projected on ground, S = opposite, A = strafe screen-left, D = strafe screen-right; pitch must not move player vertically.
- Aim: authoritative ray from camera centre (crosshair), NOT from gun barrel.
- Two zombies: A stationary, B walks slowly toward player (stops ~dist<=2.2). Both block-built humanoids, health bar over head, exactly 5 HP (5th valid hit kills, not 4th/6th), dead zombie no longer targetable.
- Evidence standard: mechanically verified vs visually inspected vs human-only must be separated in REPORT.md.

## CURRENT PRODUCT STATE
- Files: `index.html` (entry, viewport 1280x800), `game.js` (~717 lines, whole game), `three.module.js` (vendored).
- Served at http://127.0.0.1:8802/ (curl 200). Entry = index.html.
- IMPORTANT: `THREE` is NOT a page global (ES module import) — do NOT reference THREE in codex-browser eval.
- Hooks: window.__AGENT_STATE__ (player logical+world pos, camera yaw/pitch, camera forward, crosshair target, last shot hit/miss+targetId, both zombies health/positions, ready) and window.__THREE_GAME_TEST_HOOKS__ (fire, setYaw, setPitch, setPlayerPosition, setZombiePosition, resetZombieHp, respawn, setDebugLabels, setCalibrationTarget, projectToScreen, projectLogical, holdKey/releaseKey/releaseAllKeys, getCamera, getState).
- Coordinate convention (game.js): logical (x,z) -> world (x,0,-z). Spawn (0,0), yaw=0 -> fwd world (0,0,-1) = logical +Y. yaw>0 = turn right; fwd=(sin yaw,0,-cos yaw); right=(cos yaw,0,sin yaw).
- Zombies: A logical (-2.5,11) stationary; B (2.5,11) walks toward player, stops at dist<=2.2. Both HP=5.
- Runtime status: page loads, no fatal errors observed; movement/crosshair verified; AIM-RAY DEFECT OPEN (see UNRESOLVED).

## COMPLETED (mechanically verified via codex-browser eval)
1. Crosshair DOM center == viewport center (640,400) EXACT (getBoundingClientRect, re-confirmed).
2. Screen-projection proof at spawn: (0,1) ndc z=0.900 in front, sx=640 sy=1061 (front); (0,-1) behind; diagonals (-1,1) ndc.x=-0.860 left-front, (1,1) +0.860 right-front, (-1,-1)/(1,-1) behind => W front, S back, A left, D right, all 8 combos correct.
3. Movement yaw=0: W (0,+4.299), S (0,-4.298), A (-4.298,0), D (+3.999,0).
4. Camera-relative: yaw=+90deg W (+4.099,0) A (0,+4.398) D (0,-4.199); yaw=-90deg W (-3.999,0) A (0,-4.1) D (0,+4.499).
5. Pitch 0.9 + W -> player y stays 1.7 (no vertical drift).
6. Calibration target logical (0,11) h=1.7 -> screen (640,400), ndc (0,0) at yaw=0 (crosshair<->ray agreement on centre line).
7. Fixed earlier: syncCamera() stale-quaternion bug (camera.rotation reset but not quaternion -> stale aim ray). Fixed via camera.quaternion.identity() (game.js ~line 162).

## UNRESOLVED
BLOCKING: crosshairTarget() returns null in EVERY tested aim — including zombie A placed directly on the centre line at logical (0,11) with yaw=0/pitch=0, where the torso box (world x=0, y=0.85..1.6, z=-11.17..-10.83) plainly contains the centre ray. Confirmed by manual math: torso center in camera space = (0,-0.475,-10) i.e. dead-centre, in front. Manual ray math says it MUST hit, but game's crosshairTarget() AND fire() both report no hit.
Suspects to inspect: (a) zombieWorldHitboxes() rotation math / box construction (game.js ~line 323); (b) resetZombieHp/setZombiePosition not actually moving the hitbox source; (c) raycaster/aimRay() using stale camera matrix (game.js ~lines 401-420, fire ~line 475).
Debug plan: add temp hook or eval dumping zombieWorldHitboxes() boxes + ray origin/direction; compare.
This is a blocking crosshair-to-hit defect — must be FIXED, not worked around.

## LAST TEST
codex-browser eval: placed zombie A at logical (0,11), yaw=0, pitch=0, waited a frame, read __AGENT_STATE__.
Result: crosshair target = null (no hit), despite torso box provably containing the centre ray. Also verified torso center camera-space = (0,-0.475,-10) via manual transform.

## NEXT INTENDED ACTION
Debug the aim-ray bug: inspect game.js zombieWorldHitboxes (~L323), aimRay/crosshairTarget (~L401-420), fire (~L475). Add a temporary debug hook (or eval) that dumps the hitbox list + ray origin/direction, find why the ray misses the torso box, fix it. Then re-verify: aim A -> targetId 'A'; aim B -> 'B'; offset yaw -> near-miss null + fire() miss.

## SKILLS
Loaded (relevant): threejs-qa-release (test hooks __THREE_GAME_TEST_HOOK__/__AGENT_STATE__ convention, playtest-bot.md), threejs-debug-profiler (camera/input/transform debugging, scene-debugging checklist), threejs-gameplay-systems (FPS controls, camera-relative movement, raycast/hit, update order). threejs-game-ui-designer (crosshair/health bar), threejs-aaa-graphics-builder (block visuals), game-engine/game-developer (3d-web-games.md) available as needed. threejs-game-director not needed.

## EVIDENCE
- Served: http://127.0.0.1:8802/ (index.html).
- Screenshots: none yet (need to hide start overlay / pointer-lock first, then codex-browser screenshot to /tmp).
- Key verified numbers above (COMPLETED section) are the evidence base for REPORT.md.
- No screenshots/hashes committed yet.

## DO NOT REPEAT
- Do NOT accept internal consistency (HUD/labels/transform agreeing) as proof of orientation — must use screen-space projection (ndc signs / projected screen coords).
- Do NOT reference THREE in codex-browser eval (not a global).
- Do NOT read/copy code from other projects (clean room).
- codex-browser eval does NOT await Promises/async — (async()=>{...})() returns {}. Use setInterval step-driver pattern (window.__Tn={step,plan,timer}, advance ~80ms/step, then read window.__Tn.out) to wait between state changes.
- Camera re-syncs only on the next animation frame after setYaw/setPlayerPosition — always wait >=1 frame before reading __AGENT_STATE__ or firing.

