  //   and vector.set(ndcX, ndcY, -1).unproject(camera) for the far point, then dir = far - origin
  // For NDC (0,0): 
  //   near point in view space: (0, 0, -near) -> world
  //   far point in view space: (0, 0, -1) -> world (normalized)
  // So the ray direction in world space is the camera's forward vector.
  // Camera forward = -Z axis of camera = (0,0,-1) rotated by camera quaternion.
  const q = cam.quaternion;
